.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
Tokens, properties, style patches and themes\&. 

\fBPart of the host facing interface\&.\fP A host binds to \fBschultz_api\&.h\fP, which includes this header\&.
.PP
Four concepts, from the bottom up:
.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
A \fBtoken\fP is a named value such as \fCcolor\&.accent\fP or \fCspace\&.md\fP\&. Every token has a value compiled into the toolkit, so a lookup can never find a hole\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
A \fBtheme\fP is a sparse override table over those defaults\&. An empty theme is valid and means 'use the defaults throughout'\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
A \fBproperty\fP is something a node can set: background, padding, text colour\&. Each one declares whether changing it costs a repaint or a relayout\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
A \fBpatch\fP is a sparse set of property values\&. Styles, inline node style and per state style are all patches\&.
.PP
.PP
A property value is either a literal or a reference to a token\&. The token form is what lets a style follow a theme change; a literal will not\&. 
.PP
Definition in file \fBschultz_style\&.h\fP\&.
.SH "Enumeration Type Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "anonymous enum"

.PP
Named colours in a theme\&. 
.PP
\fBEnumerator\fP
.in +1c
.TP
\fB\fISCHULTZ_TOKEN_COLOR_WINDOW \fP\fP
Behind everything\&. 
.TP
\fB\fISCHULTZ_TOKEN_COLOR_SURFACE \fP\fP
A panel or control background\&. 
.TP
\fB\fISCHULTZ_TOKEN_COLOR_SURFACE_RAISED \fP\fP
A surface above another surface\&. 
.TP
\fB\fISCHULTZ_TOKEN_COLOR_SURFACE_SUNKEN \fP\fP
A surface pressed into another\&. 
.TP
\fB\fISCHULTZ_TOKEN_COLOR_ACCENT \fP\fP
The primary action colour\&. 
.TP
\fB\fISCHULTZ_TOKEN_COLOR_BORDER \fP\fP
Outline of a control\&. 
.TP
\fB\fISCHULTZ_TOKEN_COLOR_TEXT \fP\fP
Body text\&. 
.TP
\fB\fISCHULTZ_TOKEN_COLOR_TEXT_MUTED \fP\fP
Secondary text\&. 
.TP
\fB\fISCHULTZ_TOKEN_COLOR_TEXT_ON_ACCENT \fP\fP
Text drawn on the accent colour\&. 
.TP
\fB\fISCHULTZ_TOKEN_COLOR_TEXT_DISABLED \fP\fP
Text that cannot be used\&. 
.TP
\fB\fISCHULTZ_TOKEN_COLOR_FOCUS_RING \fP\fP
Ring around the focused control\&. 
.TP
\fB\fISCHULTZ_TOKEN_COLOR_SELECTION \fP\fP
Selected text or list row\&. 
.TP
\fB\fISCHULTZ_TOKEN_COLOR_DANGER \fP\fP
Destructive action\&. 
.TP
\fB\fISCHULTZ_TOKEN_COLOR_SURFACE_INVERSE \fP\fP
A surface deliberately opposite to the rest of the page, and the text that goes on it\&. Dark where the page is light and light where it is dark, so that something laid over the page reads as being in front of it rather than part of it\&. Tooltips and popovers use it\&. 
.TP
\fB\fISCHULTZ_TOKEN_COLOR_TITLE_BAR \fP\fP
The band across the top of a dialog, and the title written on it\&. 
.TP
\fB\fISCHULTZ_TOKEN_COLOR_SCROLL_TRACK \fP\fP
A scroll bar's groove, and the part of it that moves\&. These are their own colours rather than borrowed ones because the two have to stay apart from each other, and a token that means something else is free to drift until they meet\&. 
.TP
\fB\fISCHULTZ_TOKEN_COLOR_SHADOW \fP\fP
The colour a drop shadow is drawn in\&. Black at an alpha, rather than a grey, so that it darkens whatever it falls on instead of tinting it\&.
.PP
It is a theme's colour because how heavy a shadow is says as much about a design as a surface tone does, and because a shadow needs a different strength on a dark page than on a light one to read as the same depth\&.
.PP
Nothing carries a shadow unless it is asked to: SCHULTZ_PROP_SHADOW_COLOR still defaults to transparent, and this is the colour to reach for when a host wants one\&. 
.TP
\fB\fISCHULTZ_TOKEN_COLOR_TRANSPARENT \fP\fP
Fully transparent\&. 
.TP
\fB\fISCHULTZ_TOKEN_COLOR_COUNT \fP\fP
How many colour tokens exist\&. 
